# File-size budget (scripts/file-size.py, `just file-size`): a first-party .rs
# file has at most `limit` lines, a test file (under a `tests/` directory, a
# `tests.rs` or `*_tests.rs` module) at most `test-limit`. Each entry below is
# a file that was already over its limit, with its size when it was listed: it
# may shrink, never grow. `just file-size-update` lowers an entry when its file
# shrinks and removes it once the file is under its limit; no entry is ever
# raised or added. A file over its budget is split into modules.
limit 500
test-limit 800
ext .rs
# No generated or fixture .rs file is tracked; one would go here as
# `exclude <path glob>`.

